id: pm-rl-0x9x
title: Bound concurrent checkpoint fixture contention without losing promotions
description: "Investigate release CI checkpoint promotion lock conflict from GitHub issue #152; characterize loaded contention, preserve declared bounds and checkpoint roots, and prove any correction by behavioral revert."
type: Issue
pm_format_version: 2
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[1]: "gh:unbraind/pm-rl#152"
created_at: "2026-11-07T15:24:16.420Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-07T21:53:39.377Z"
author: codex-agent
comments[19]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-07T15:25:02.608Z",codex-agent,"Read issue #152 and SDK issue #1516 including all comments. No synced match exists, so this item owns gh:unbraind/pm-rl#152. Baseline focused real-process checkpoint fixture passed 1/1 under existing host load. The shipped bounded-contention contract explicitly permits lock_conflict; the installed SDK exposes CommitWorkspaceTransactionOptions.lockWaitMs, so this is not a missing wait API. Next: 30 instrumented repetitions under one low-priority CPU burner, then deterministic live-holder timing and a behavioral revert proof. Full multi-hour npm/Bun release gates are delegated to CI by the task instruction."
  "2026-11-07T15:31:16.871Z",codex-agent,"Controlled live-holder reproduction failed 1/1 with the original 30000 ms fixture wait: a healthy parent holds sdk-workspace-transaction for 35000 ms; a waiting promoter reports lock_conflict/lock_owner_alive after 30007 ms (another waiter is serialized behind the approval preflight lock). This demonstrates an insufficient positive-fixture bound, not lock corruption or lost committed writes. Testing a fixture-only 120000 ms wait, aligned with its existing 120000 ms fit signal and inside its unchanged 900000 ms outer deadline. Production lock defaults, retry contracts, trainer budgets and pinned SDK remain unchanged. The unforced instrumented baseline remains at its original 30000 ms wait until all 30 repetitions finish."
  "2026-11-07T15:34:31.519Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof: in a disposable source copy, change only concurrentCheckpointPromotions waitMs default from 120000 to 30000 and run Node 26.13.0: node --test --test-concurrency=2 --test-name-pattern=\"outwait a healthy\" test/checkpoint-artifacts.test.ts. It fails 1/1 with SDK lock_conflict, lock_owner_alive, waited_ms=30006. The fixed 120000 ms implementation passed 1/1 on Node 24.19.0 and 1/1 on Node 26.13.0 before this revert; rerun the fixed test after all edits. Both promoters retain their original job identities, exactly one training charge each, both promoted roots and the single verified shared artifact. No SDK defect is established and no upstream issue should be filed."
  "2026-11-07T15:43:26.190Z",codex-agent,"Supplemental local health gate found a separate extension host version mismatch (pinned host 2026.11.3 versus automatically resolved pm-github host floor 2026.11.6); recorded with existing follow-up pm-rl-9uz4 instead of duplicating it. Tracker integrity and history drift checks pass. No history rewrite or dependency bump is part of this fix. The linked snapshot test command passes 2/2, including the fixed live-holder regression after the disposable revert proof."
  "2026-11-07T15:45:40.203Z",codex-agent,"Loaded baseline complete: 30/30 focused invocations pass, zero failures and zero lock_conflict reports, using Node 24.19.0, V8 test coverage, test-concurrency=2, and one low-priority CPU burner on the shared host. The original 30000 ms admission bound was retained throughout. This is an honest non-reproduction of the spontaneous hosted failure; the controlled 35000 ms live-holder case and revert proof demonstrate fixture scheduling sensitivity separately. The matching 30-run fixed-bound series has now started."
  "2026-11-07T15:47:53.419Z",codex-agent,"Final fixture behavioral revert repeated on Node 26.13.0: changing only PM_LOCK_WAIT_MS from 120000 back to 30000 in a disposable copy fails 1/1 with lock_conflict/lock_owner_alive, waited_ms=30085 on the approval lock queued behind the held workspace mutex. CI-style isolated health passes with only pre-existing advisories. Main advanced to release commit 25b4011; its authored runtime delta is only the version constant, and the branch fast-forwards to that release without changing dependency pins or checkpoint behavior."
  "2026-11-07T15:52:49.322Z",codex-agent,"Final source after the release fast-forward passes the linked snapshot command on Node 26.13.0: 2 tests, 2 passed, zero failed/skipped/canceled/todo. This run follows the final literal-only behavioral revert and uses the fixed 120000 ms wait in both positive fixtures. The controlled case verifies the live holder lease remains byte-identical until release, original identities and exactly-once training charges, both promotion roots, and verified shared-artifact retention. No new pm CLI/SDK bug was established; the development health warning disappears under CI-style home isolation."
  "2026-11-07T16:06:26.978Z",codex-agent,"Final loaded result: before 0 failures / 30 runs; after 0 failures / 30 runs. All 60 instrumented Node 24.19.0 invocations pass without skip/cancel/todo or lock_conflict under one low-priority CPU burner, with test-concurrency=2. This does not reproduce or estimate the spontaneous hosted failure rate. Controlled final Node 26.13.0 sensitivity: original wait fails 1/1 after 30085 ms against a live owner; fixed wait passes 1/1, and the complete linked snapshot command passes 2/2 after the revert and release fast-forward. Classification (a): the positive fixture admission bound was below healthy instrumented contention; no pm-rl integrity defect or additional SDK defect is established. Build, typecheck, test compilation and lint pass; docstrings report 539 documented declarations across 62 sources, duplication is zero, and CI-style strict health passes with existing advisories. The 120000 ms fixture wait preserves existing fit/outer deadlines and all receipt, identity, accounting, root and artifact assertions. Full npm/Bun release gates are pending CI under the task instruction; no full coverage or release certification is claimed. See docs/checkpoint-contention.md. Ready for one PR fixing #152; leave this item in progress for orchestrator verification."
  "2026-11-07T17:03:37.621Z",codex-agent,"Resumed PR #158 review round 1. Worktree is clean at 63cc6cd and main is already an ancestor, so no merge is needed. Both inline findings and the additional review-body timing note identify one class: a contention regression must observe a real acquisition attempt and measure its blocked interval, rather than infer contention from child readiness or an owner timer. Search all package lock-contention tests and exposed SDK/CLI/packed surfaces for the same rule; add a delayed-before-attempt adversarial case and behavioral revert evidence. Preserve the completed 60-run evidence without rerunning it. The new instruction requires full npm and Bun gates sequentially with at most two workers, and explicitly authorizes a review-response comment and new review request."
  "2026-11-07T17:08:11.673Z",codex-agent,"Class audit complete: reviewed all package TypeScript timer/delay and lock call sites, SDK adapters in state-boundary.ts, index.ts, checkpoint-artifacts.ts and evaluation-plan.ts; lock tests in sdk-adoption, sdk-lock-confinement, state-boundary, lineage, sequential-evaluation and evaluation-plan; process/controller heartbeat and polling barriers; acceptance/packed and compatibility consumers including JSON/TOON and no-git fixtures. Only concurrentCheckpointPromotions inferred a minimum contention wait from readiness plus a parent release timer. Other lock refusals execute real operations while an owner is explicitly held; heartbeat/polling timers assert observed state, not acquisition duration. The fix observes real failed native lock-file opens in the child, requires a monotonic blocked witness beyond 35000 ms before parent release, and checks the successful acquisition duration. Both children deliberately delay fitting by 8000 ms after go, exceeding the former five-second margin. Real SDK operations and filesystem calls are retained; this is observation, not an SDK mock. The first targeted attempt reached both successful publications but exposed an obsolete array destructure after switching filtered IPC receipts to objects; corrected it and rerunning focused tests before full gates."
  "2026-11-07T17:12:24.807Z",codex-agent,"Review regression proof passes in two independent disposable copies. Variant old-wait changes only PM_LOCK_WAIT_MS from 120000 to 30000: focused outwait test fails with lock_conflict. Variant readiness-timer restores parent timer-based release (35000 ms after readiness), retaining the new successful-acquisition oracle: with the eight-second pre-fit delay it fails specifically at \"a successful real acquisition must have waited beyond the old thirty-second limit\". Thus the oracle catches the timing class independently of the chosen lock wait. Real implementation was never mutated; temporary copies were removed. Focused tests passed 2/2 before these mutations; rerun the unchanged fixed implementation through pinned pm now, then execute full npm and Bun release gates sequentially with two workers."
  "2026-11-07T17:14:02.083Z",codex-agent,"Post-revert pinned snapshot regression passes on Node 26.13.0: 2/2, zero failures/skips/cancellations/todo, including the delayed-start measured-acquisition case. Test compilation and whole-package lint pass. Both independent behavioral reverts fail at their intended oracle. Starting complete npm release:check with CI-style isolated home/Git configuration and two workers, then the complete Bun gate sequentially; no threshold or source-scope changes."
  "2026-11-07T18:19:31.509Z",codex-agent,"Complete npm gate has exposed an unrelated existing HTTP recovery failure: the unchanged crash drill times out at 300005.355292 ms and subsequent receipt cases fail. A retained idle HTTP worker was independently sampled for CPU/I/O inactivity and only that worker was terminated so remaining results can finish. Existing follow-up pm-rl-local-gate-timing records it; no duplicate issue and no timeout/assertion changes. Both checkpoint cases pass in the full covered run (ordinary promotion 23606.637734 ms, acquisition-witness case 68532.932632 ms). The npm gate is unaccepted and still collecting the rest; Bun will run afterward."
  "2026-11-07T18:35:08.840Z",codex-agent,The ongoing full npm gate also reports the known packed LM CLI timing case failing after 35734.588011 ms total test wall (not measured CLI duration). Existing pm-rl-7c7m records it; no duplicate item or deadline change. Current review correction remains confined to checkpoint test synchronization and real acquisition observation. Complete npm results and the sequential Bun attempt are still pending.
  "2026-11-07T20:00:29.617Z",codex-agent,"Full npm release:check completed exit 1 after 9897 seconds, unchanged two-worker scope: release policies 31/31 pass; coverage suite 1511 total, 1504 pass, 6 fail, 1 cancellation, zero skip/todo. Both checkpoint regressions pass. Exact footer: unchanged HTTP crash drill cancelled at 300000 ms, five subsequent HTTP cases fail uv_cwd after cleanup, packed LM child reaches existing 25000 ms ETIMEDOUT. No full-gate or coverage certification is claimed. Bun full gate follows; local Bun 1.3.5 differs from CI pin 1.3.14, so checking an isolated official pinned runtime without changing package pins or the installed runtime."
  "2026-11-07T20:08:23.225Z",codex-agent,"Sequential full Bun validation now uses the official CI-pinned Bun 1.3.14 archive in an isolated temporary runtime; SHA256 951ee2aee855f08595aeec6225226a298d3fea83a3dcd6465c09cbccdf7e848f matches the official release metadata. Installed Bun 1.3.5 and all package pins remain unchanged. Both changed checkpoint cases pass in this full covered run (ordinary 11992.960601 ms; delayed-start measured-acquisition 59903.034954 ms). No Bun failure has been reported at this checkpoint; full gate is still in progress and not certified. Saved behavioral-revert diagnostics were also independently checked for exact typed lock_conflict/lock_owner_alive context and the intended ERR_ASSERTION, not merely matching source text."
  "2026-11-07T20:34:16.819Z",codex-agent,"The pinned Bun 1.3.14 full gate passes the complete HTTP recovery file, including the crash drill and interrupted-before-dispatch cases that failed in npm. It now reports the separately owned packed LM CLI case as its sole failure so far, at 23619.436248 ms total test wall including setup. Do not interpret that as measured CLI duration; exact footer is pending. Both measured checkpoint regressions remain passed. Full Bun still collecting; no gate certification and no source/timeout changes."
  "2026-11-07T21:51:51.494Z",codex-agent,"All three review notes are addressed by the same class correction: minimum contention evidence is measured from real failed native opens, not readiness or a parent timer. The package-wide audit found no other positive minimum-wait assumption. An eight-second delayed fit still requires a blocked witness beyond 35000 ms before parent release and a matching successful-acquisition duration; lossless job/charge/root/artifact checks remain. Focused post-revert Node 26 pinned snapshot passes 2/2; both independent reverts fail their intended typed SDK conflict or acquisition-duration assertion. Full npm: policy 31/31, suite 1511 total /1504 pass/6 fail/1 cancellation/0 skip. Full CI-pinned Bun 1.3.14: policy31/31, suite1511/1510 pass/1 fail/0 cancellation/0 skip. Both checkpoint cases pass in both full suites. npm fails existing HTTP drill/uv_cwd cases (pm-rl-local-gate-timing) and the LM child timeout; Bun only fails measured CLI20104ms versus20000ms (pm-rl-7c7m). Neither full gate is certified; thresholds, source scope and unrelated tests are unchanged. Temporary Bun archive matched official SHA256 and is removed; installed runtime and dependency pins unchanged. Remaining static/artifact checks and PR response/new review request follow."
  "2026-11-07T21:53:38.578Z",codex-agent,"Review correction is complete and source is unchanged since both full validations. Post-gate identity audit passes, production audit finds zero vulnerabilities, package dry-run passes with 260 files, and changelog check passes. The official temporary Bun runtime is removed and installed Bun still reports 1.3.5. Both source-focused tests pass after two independently verified behavioral reverts; both also pass in each full covered suite. Full npm and Bun remain failed for the exact existing HTTP/CLI cases recorded above; no full-coverage, release or review approval is claimed. Ready to commit/push the same PR #158, answer both inline threads plus the additional review-body note and request fresh CodeRabbit review as explicitly instructed. Fresh exact-head CI and review remain required at https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rl/pull/158/checks . Preserve completed 60-run evidence; leave this item in progress for orchestrator verification."
